DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssyyssaarrcchh() system call performs the architecture-dependent function
     specified by _n_u_m_b_e_r with the arguments specified by the _a_r_g_s pointer.
     The _a_r_g_s argument is a pointer to a structure defining the actual argu‐
     ments of the function.  Symbolic constants and argument structures for
     the architecture-dependent functions can be found in the header file
     <_m_a_c_h_i_n_e_/_s_y_s_a_r_c_h_._h>.

     The ssyyssaarrcchh() system call should never be called directly by user pro‐
     grams.  Instead, they should access its functions using the architecture-
     dependent library.

